title: Cornered behind a locked door — silence remains
story: ides-of-march
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: The jest answer to the poet's plain question walks him out
  of the scene — but behind a locked tiring-house door the world
  refuses the exit: the row is withheld whole and the default evasion
  stands, because silence is the one move that can never be taken
  away. The door is locked BEFORE the question opens, since the
  question is asked once.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/ides-of-march/chord/ides-of-march.story
    stories/ides-of-march/tests/transcripts/cornered-locked.transcript

---

> north
[OK: contains "Stage"]

> west
[OK: contains "Tiring-House"]

# Turn the key on the only door out of this room first.
> take the key
[OK: contains "Taken"]

> close the door
[OK: contains "close"]

> lock the door with the key
[OK: contains "lock"]

> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "The new hired man"]

# The book talk opens, question on its heels.
> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "So it is not carried"]

# The answer that would walk him out is refused whole by the world —
# the default evasion stands in its place.
> ask shakespeare about a spy
[OK: contains "I don't know anything about that"]
[OK: not contains "given in jest"]
